! I103: si8-lelfield.in on the PAW dataset Si.pbe-n-kjpaw_psl.0.1.UPF (ecutrho = 160, as
! si8-us-pbe.in), with the k-list cut to two strings of nppstr = 5 along z at
! (0, 0) and (1/2, 1/2). The references are pw.x 7.5 (serial, D22) run as QE's
! pw_electric chain at conv_thr = 1e-11: the plain SCF, the Berry operator at
! efield = 0 (reference.out.si8-paw-lelfield-zero) and the field at 0.001
! (reference.out.si8-paw-lelfield), and 0.002 (reference.out.si8-paw-lelfield-2),
! each from the state before it. Along z pw.x 7.5 is NOT the reference for the physics:
! compute_qqc (upflib/qvan2.f90) takes |q|^2 = q(1)^2 + q(2)^2 + q(1)^2, which is 0 for
! q = dk along z, so pw.x uses Q_ij(0) e^{-i dk.tau} for the cross augmentation. These
! outputs pin that reading of pw.x; si8-paw-lelfield-y.in is the comparison.
 &control
    calculation='scf'
    gdir=3,
    nppstr=5,
    lelfield=.true.,
    nberrycyc=3
    tprnfor=.true.
 /
 &system
    ibrav= 1, 
    celldm(1)=10.18, 
    nat=  8,
    ntyp= 1,
    ecutwfc = 20.0, ecutrho = 160.0,
    nosym=.true.
 /
 &electrons
    conv_thr = 1.0d-11,
    mixing_beta = 0.5,
    startingwfc='random',
    efield=0.001
 /
ATOMIC_SPECIES
 Si  28.086 Si.pbe-n-kjpaw_psl.0.1.UPF
ATOMIC_POSITIONS (alat)
 Si -0.123 -0.123 -0.123
 Si  0.377  0.377 -0.123
 Si  0.377 -0.123  0.377
 Si -0.123  0.377  0.377
 Si  0.123  0.123  0.123
 Si  0.623  0.623  0.123
 Si  0.623  0.123  0.623
 Si  0.123  0.623  0.623
K_POINTS
 10
  0.0  0.0  0.000000000 1
  0.0  0.0  0.200000000 1
  0.0  0.0  0.400000000 1
  0.0  0.0  0.600000000 1
  0.0  0.0  0.800000000 1
  0.5  0.5  0.000000000 1
  0.5  0.5  0.200000000 1
  0.5  0.5  0.400000000 1
  0.5  0.5  0.600000000 1
  0.5  0.5  0.800000000 1
